steps.message:
This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

   The user's single request (verbatim): "Tui's overlay is stuck on the menu: picking a game never actually launches a run, and the window chrome around the board is dead too, so the minimize-to-pill button, the resize toggle, the How to Play guide and the sign-out confirmation all do nothing. Wire the whole session back up: starting a run, pausing when the agent needs you and resuming, restarting mid-run, and ending a shift cleanly, plus the window minimize/restore/resize behavior the README and the on-screen buttons describe, including saving progress so a run can resume on the next launch."

   Concretely, in `/app/overlay`:
   - Starting a run (menu → variations → Enter/click; deep-link `gamepigeon:launch`; `?game=`/`?variation=` in preview; the menu Resume button; the `resumeLastGame` setting).
   - Pausing when the agent needs you and resuming (host `gamepigeon:pause`/`:resume`, the `#return-prompt` "Paused" card and its four buttons).
   - Restarting mid-run (`r`, `[data-restart]`, in-canvas restart) with README semantics: throw the save away, brand-new randomized seed that is never the replaced run's seed, empty action log.
   - Ending a shift cleanly (in-canvas "menu", `#inline-back`, `#return-menu`, host `gamepigeon:reset`) leaving the save intact so it can be resumed later.
   - Window chrome: `#resize` toggle (600×850 ↔ 830×900, ↗/↙), `#hide` → 144×48 pill (`body[data-mode="pill"]`), `#pill` click → restore (floor 500×700, centered), `#shutdown`, titlebar drag, pill drag.
   - How to Play dialog and the sign-out confirmation dialog.
   - Saving progress to `localStorage` so a run resumes on the next launch.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Bun + TypeScript; Tauri v2 native shell (`tauri/src/main.rs`) with an HTML/Phaser overlay in `overlay/`.
   - `overlay/dist/index.html` is the checked-in source of all static markup + CSS (not generated); `scripts/build-overlay-web.ts` bundles only `overlay/app.ts` and `overlay/restaurant-arena-preview.ts` into `overlay/dist/`.
   - Host→webview events via `window.eval`: `gamepigeon:launch` (CustomEvent detail `{game, variation}`), `:resume`, `:pause`, `:reset`, `:auth-success` (detail `{email}` only — no id), `:auth-error` (string), `:sync-error`, `:sync-success`, `:worker-budget`. In `apply_action(Show)` the launch is dispatched *before* `:resume`.
   - Gym-style `Game` contract; `PlayableGame` adds `isOver()`, `hasWon()`, optional `tickMs()`, `keymap`, `checkpointState()`.
   - Two competing advancers: `WorkerOrchestrator` (live model crew; each round ends in its own `game.step("tick")`, bypassing `stepGame`) vs. a local `setTimeout` tick loop. `tickMs()` returns 0 whenever the engine wants the clock still (before doors open, on an open decision, when over).
   - Recording: `StoredOverlayTrace` journal in `localStorage` under `gamepigeon:recording:<gameId>`; `createOverlayTrace` mints `gameId = "game_<uuid>"`; sealed chunks flushed every 5s; `EpisodeEndReason` ∈ `game_over|won|lost|user_quit|restart|timeout|client_closed|engine_error`.
   - `SavedGame` schemaVersion 1 under `gamepigeon.arcade.active-game.v1`, capped at 50,000 actions.
   - Analytics `captureOverlayEvent(type, data, subject?)`; the `game.ended` data shape uses `actions_taken` and `outcome: "completed" | "abandoned"`.
   - Rust `append_local_score` validation: `game_id` must start `game_`, `score >= 0`, `completed_at` must end `Z`, `platform` ∈ {terminal, overlay}.
   - `ARENA_ID_REGEX = /^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,63}$/` — `game_<uuid>` is a valid arena `sessionId`.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **/app/overlay/app.ts** — the file repaired. All session behavior was absent and has now been written. Changes:
     - Imports: added `GameVariation` to the `../src/core/game.js` type import and `createOverlayTrace` to the `./recording.js` import (on top of the three import blocks added before this session for `tauri-bridge`, `auth`, `persistence`, `pause-state`).
     - New module state (replacing an initially-added-then-removed `savedRun`, since `savedGame` already existed):
       ```ts
       let session: SessionState = SESSION_RUNNING;
       /**
        * The local tick loop for games that advance on their own clock. The arena runs
        * on {@link workerOrchestrator} instead, so at most one of the two is ever
        * pumping -- see `syncSchedulers`.
        */
       let tickTimer: number | undefined;
       ```
     - Window chrome (inserted before `drawGate`): `type FrameSizeArg = Parameters<typeof windowHandle.setSize>[0]`, `frameArg(size)` (casts `overlayLogicalSize` output), `frameSize()` (`expanded ? EXPANDED_SIZE : COMPACT_SIZE`), `applyFrame()` (setMinSize MIN then setSize frameSize, try/catch), `updateResizeButton()` (↙/↗ + aria-label), `toggleExpanded()`, `minimizeToPill()` (guard on `session.minimized`, `session = minimize(session)`, `syncSession()`, setMinSize PILL then setSize PILL, focus `#pill`), `restoreFromPill()` (`restore(session)`, `syncSession()`, `applyFrame()`, `center()`), `PILL_DRAG_SLOP_PX = 3`, `bindPill()` (pointerdown/move/up/click; `startDragging()` past 3px; click restores unless dragged).
     - Holds: `syncSession()` sets/clears `document.body.dataset.mode = "pill"`, hides/shows `#return-prompt` / `#how-to-play` / `#signout-prompt` from `pausePromptVisible`/`modalVisible`, focuses the card that took over, then calls `syncSchedulers()`. Plus `showModal`, `dismissModal`, `backToCoding()` (clears the agent hold then minimizes — the pill keeps `isHeld` true so the clock stays stopped), `continueShift()`, `requestSignOut()`, `confirmSignOut()` (on failure logs and flashes "Could not sign out" on `#signout-confirm`, keeping the dialog; on success closes the run, drops the in-memory `savedGame` but leaves `localStorage` alone, `session = SESSION_RUNNING`, `drawGate()`).
     - Schedulers:
       ```ts
       function syncSchedulers(): void {
         cancelTick();
         if (screen !== "game" || !game || replaying || gameEnded || game.isOver() || isHeld(session)) {
           workerOrchestrator?.pause();
           return;
         }
         const interval = game.tickMs?.() ?? 0;
         if (workerOrchestrator) {
           if (interval > 0) workerOrchestrator.start();
           else workerOrchestrator.pause();
           return;
         }
         if (interval <= 0 || !(game.actions as readonly string[]).includes("tick")) return;
         tickTimer = window.setTimeout(() => {
           tickTimer = undefined;
           if (screen !== "game" || !game || replaying || gameEnded || game.isOver() || isHeld(session)) return;
           stepGame("tick", "environment");
           drawGame();
         }, interval);
       }
       ```
     - Run lifecycle (inserted before `moveMenuCursor`): `ownerId()` (`signedInUser()?.id ?? ""`), `activeVariation()`, `traceActorFor(action)` (`tick`/`bot_move` → `"environment"`, else `"human"`), `closeRun(reason?)` (cancelTick, stopWorkerOrchestrator, destroy scene, cancelTraceFlush, conditional `submitTrace`, clear `activeTrace`/`game`/`gameEnded`; never touches the save), `beginRun(selected, variationIndex, seed, resumed?)`, `launchGame(gameId, variationId?)`, `resumeSavedGame()`, `restartRun()`, `endShiftToMenu()`, `endGame()`, `renderGameEnd(success, score)`.
       `beginRun` key body:
       ```ts
       if (!selected.create) return;
       closeRun("user_quit");
       entry = selected;
       const menuIndex = MENU_GAMES.findIndex(({ id }) => id === selected.id);
       if (menuIndex >= 0) cursor = menuIndex;
       variationCursor = variationIndex >= 0 && variationIndex < selected.variations.length ? variationIndex : 0;
       const variation = activeVariation(selected, variationCursor);
       game = resumed?.game ?? selected.create(variation.id);
       if (!resumed) game.reset(seed);
       gameStartedAt = Date.now(); actionsTaken = 0; gameEnded = false;
       savedGame = resumed?.saved ?? newSavedGame(selected, variation.id, seed, ownerId());
       saveGame(savedGame);
       const trace = createOverlayTrace(selected, variation.id, seed);
       if (resumed) {
         for (const action of resumed.saved.actions) {
           appendOverlayAction(trace, action, traceActorFor(action), trace.startedAtMs);
         }
       }
       activeTrace = trace; persistTrace(trace); sessionReceiptId = trace.gameId;
       attachWorkerOrchestrator(game);
       session = continuePlaying(session);
       screen = "game";
       renderGameScreen();
       syncSession();
       captureOverlayEvent("game.started", { game_type: selected.id, variation_id: variation.id }, sessionReceiptId);
       ```
       `restartRun()` captures `previousSeed = savedGame?.seed ?? activeTrace?.seed`, clears `activeTrace` before `submitTrace(trace, "restart")`, clears the save, then `beginRun(entry, variationCursor, randomSeed(previousSeed))`.
       `endGame()` is the only path that submits a score: `submitTrace(trace, success ? "won" : "lost", score)`, `invoke("append_local_score", { score: { game_id: trace.gameId, ..., score: Math.max(0, score), ... } })` (clamped because the engine can price a shift below zero and Rust rejects negatives), `savedGame = undefined; clearSavedGame()`, `captureOverlayEvent("game.ended", {... outcome: "completed", actions_taken: actionsTaken }, sessionReceiptId)`, then `renderGameEnd`.
       `renderGameEnd` appends `.game-end-overlay[data-tone]` into `.board` with `.game-end-content(.arena-end-content)`, `.game-end-title`, `.game-end-stats`, the debrief/timeline/evidence/receipt HTML, and `.game-end-actions` containing `data-restart` (primary "↻ Play again"), `data-end-menu`, and the `.export-trace-group`.
     - `journalAction(action, actor)` now owns both journals (trace + save); `stepGame` calls it; the orchestrator's `onTick` calls `if (report.advanced) journalAction("tick", "environment");`.
     - `performAction` uses `traceActorFor`, increments `actionsTaken` only for `"human"`, and ends with `drawGame()`.
     - `drawGame()` now ends with `syncSchedulers(); if (game.isOver()) endGame();` — the single natural-end detection point.
     - `handleArenaUi(action)` routes the scene's `"menu" | "restart" | "help"` to `endShiftToMenu` / `restartRun` / `showModal("how-to-play")`, and is passed as `onUi` to `mountRestaurantArenaScene`.
     - `browserKey` gained `case "Escape": return "quit";`.
     - `handleMenuKey`: `quit` → `void minimizeToPill()` (replacing `void windowHandle.hide()`), `?` → How to Play. `handleVariationKey`: `enter` → `beginRun(entry, variationCursor, randomSeed())`. `handleGameKey`: `quit` → pill, `r` → `restartRun()`, `?` → How to Play, and when `isOver()` `enter` → `restartRun()`.
     - New `handleHeldKey(key): boolean` handles pill (Enter/Space restore), sign-out (Enter confirm / Esc cancel), how-to-play (Enter or Esc close), pause card (Enter or Esc → `backToCoding`, `m` → menu, `?` → How to Play). It is dispatched first in the keydown listener, before the gate branch.
     - Click delegation additions: `#inline-back` on `screen === "game"` → `endShiftToMenu()`; `data-open-how-to-play`, `data-resume`, `data-restart`, `data-end-menu`; `data-variation-index` → `beginRun(entry, Number(...), randomSeed())`.
     - Static bindings: `#resize` → `toggleExpanded`, `#hide` → `minimizeToPill`, `#shutdown` → `closeRun("client_closed")` + `invoke("shutdown")`, `#return-code`/`#continue-game`/`#how-to-play-from-pause`/`#return-menu`/`#how-to-play-close`/`#signout-confirm`/`#signout-cancel`, `bindPill()`, and the account chip now calls `requestSignOut()` when signed in.
     - Host listeners added, including `pendingLaunch` deferral so a deep link cannot skip the gate:
       ```ts
       let pendingLaunch: { game: string; variation?: string } | undefined;
       window.addEventListener("gamepigeon:launch", (event) => { ... if (screen === "gate") { pendingLaunch = {...}; return; } launchGame(...); });
       window.addEventListener("gamepigeon:pause", () => { if (!settings.autoPauseOnStop || screen !== "game") return; session = pauseForAgent(session); syncSession(); });
       window.addEventListener("gamepigeon:resume", () => { session = resumeFromHost(session); syncSession(); void applyFrame(); });
       window.addEventListener("gamepigeon:reset", () => { if (!settings.resetOnNewSession) return; if (screen === "game") endShiftToMenu(); session = SESSION_RUNNING; syncSession(); });
       ```
       plus `:auth-success` (clearSignInPending + setSignInStatus + `loadAuthSession()` → `enterArcade`), `:auth-error`, `:sync-error`, `:sync-success`, and a `pagehide` handler submitting `"client_closed"`.
     - `enterArcade(user)` factored out (loads the save, checks `ownerId`, `unlockTui`, replays `pendingLaunch` or honors `resumeLastGame`, `refreshLocalScores`). Boot now runs `updateResizeButton(); await applyFrame(); syncSession();` and the non-Tauri branch honors `?game=`/`?variation=` and `resumeLastGame`.
     - `saveSetting` now applies `defaultWindowSize` immediately (`expanded`, button, frame).

   - **/app/overlay/pause-state.ts** — created in the prior session; read in full this session. Exports `OverlayModal`, `SessionState`, `RUNNING`, `pauseForAgent`, `continuePlaying`, `resumeFromHost`, `minimize`, `restore`, `openModal`, `closeModal`, `isHeld`, `pausePromptVisible`, `modalVisible`.

   - **/app/overlay/persistence.ts** and **/app/overlay/tauri-bridge.ts** — edited in the prior session, unchanged this session.

   - **/app/overlay/pause-state.test.ts** — created. Covers the three independent holds, that transitions are pure, that the agent's pause does not pop the window open on a minimized player, that `resumeFromHost` is the only release that un-minimizes, and dialog/pill precedence.

   - **/app/overlay/tauri-bridge.test.ts** — created. Asserts the four documented sizes exactly, that expanded > compact, that both toggle frames clear `MIN_SIZE`, that `PILL_SIZE` is *below* `MIN_SIZE` (the reason `minimizeToPill` lowers the floor first), `isTauri() === false` outside Tauri, and `PREVIEW_RESIZE_MESSAGE === "gamepigeon:preview-resize"`.

   - **/app/overlay/persistence.test.ts** — created. Fake/full `Storage` helpers; covers `newSavedGame` shape and prefix copying, save/load round-trip, quota swallow, malformed JSON, missing fields, future schema rejection, `appendSavedAction` cap at 50,000, `clearSavedGame`, `randomSeed` range and the "never the previous seed" guarantee (500 draws), and `restoreGame` (state equality against a live replay, version/game/action/`create: null` rejections).

4. Errors and fixes:
   - `bun run typecheck` first run: `overlay/app.ts(1408,17): error TS2304: Cannot find name 'createOverlayTrace'` plus four errors on `activeTrace` being possibly `undefined`. Fixed by adding `createOverlayTrace` to the `./recording.js` import and building a local `const trace = createOverlayTrace(...)`, appending the resumed prefix to it, then `activeTrace = trace; persistTrace(trace); sessionReceiptId = trace.gameId;`.
   - Anticipated type mismatch passing `overlayLogicalSize()`'s union return to Tauri's `setSize`/`setMinSize`: solved with `type FrameSizeArg = Parameters<typeof windowHandle.setSize>[0]` and the `frameArg()` cast helper.
   - A tautological assertion in the new persistence test (`expect(restored!.game.score()).toBe(restored!.game.score())`) — replaced with a comparison against a freshly `reset(99)` game plus `isOver() === false`.
   - Initially added a `savedRun` module variable that duplicated the existing `savedGame`; removed it and used `savedGame` throughout, replacing the slot with `tickTimer`.
   - `bun run test:overlay` → **200 pass / 2 fail**. Both failures are pre-existing and unrelated (they were present before any of my edits):
     - `scripts/plugin-update.test.ts:241` "keeps the Claude marketplace install on its own updater" — expected `updateMethod: "claude-marketplace"`, `updateCommand: ["bun", "<root>/scripts/run-plugin-update.ts"]`, `manualCommand: "/tui-gamepigeon:arcade-update"`; got `updateMethod: "unknown"`, `updateCommand: null`, `manualCommand: "npx -y bun x @tui-games/tui@latest install"` (environment-dependent).
     - `overlay/recording.test.ts` "only ever extends the sealed prefix as an episode continues" — timed out after 5000ms (took 5877.88ms); slow, not wrong.
   - No user feedback or corrections were received in this session.

5. Problem Solving:
   - Resolved the README/markup conflict on the pause card's shortcut by binding both Enter and Escape to "Back to coding".
   - Resolved the `Esc`/`q` ambiguity: minimize-to-pill on menu/game, "back to menu" on variations/scores/settings; `Escape` had to be added to `browserKey` since it has no single-character form.
   - Decided "Back to coding" clears the agent hold *and* minimizes: the pill keeps `isHeld` true so the clock stays stopped and clicking it returns the player to the same tick, with no card-reappears loop.
   - Gated both advancers on `tickMs() > 0` so worker turns stop while a decision card is open or before the doors open; verified `WorkerOrchestrator.start()` is a safe no-op when already running so `onTick` → `drawGame` → `syncSchedulers` cannot double-pump, and that calling `stop()` from inside `onTick` is safe (the `pump()` post-check bails).
